const issues = [
{title:"Scope subprocess environments to validation and worker needs",body:`Approved repository validation scripts and coding workers receive the full parent environment through the shared process runner. This gives repository-owned code access to evaluation-provider credentials and other unrelated ambient credentials. The relevant paths are [the shared spawn boundary](https://github.com/petercr/jev-orchestrator/blob/1547e2727d3dacc4b6ce885f47c5cb11fa7c21f9/src/process.ts#L41-L53) and [validation and worker dispatch](https://github.com/petercr/jev-orchestrator/blob/1547e2727d3dacc4b6ce885f47c5cb11fa7c21f9/src/orchestration/execute.ts#L186-L252).

## Acceptance criteria

- Build a minimal, explicit environment for each subprocess role. Keep evaluation-only credentials and their aliases in the evaluator. Preserve runtime variables needed to find supported tools, and scope any supported worker credentials to the corresponding adapter.
- Construct environments locally at execution and keep values out of candidates, worker prompts, saved runs, and traces. Preserve manual approval, Codex sandbox and networking settings, and process cleanup.
- Add offline tests at the spawn boundary using synthetic values. Verify that validation and each worker receive only their intended environment, including coverage for known provider aliases and an unrelated credential-shaped variable.`},
{title:"Keep trace writes bound to private, verified storage",body:`The trace writer creates the trace directory without checking its identity, allocates an exclusive file, then reopens the pathname for the decision record and for each orchestration append. A redirected or replaced path can send records outside the trace directory or modify another file. Trace records can contain task and repository details even after redaction, and default permissions can expose them on shared machines. See [trace allocation and decision writes](https://github.com/petercr/jev-orchestrator/blob/1547e2727d3dacc4b6ce885f47c5cb11fa7c21f9/src/logging/trace.ts#L216-L250) and [orchestration appends](https://github.com/petercr/jev-orchestrator/blob/1547e2727d3dacc4b6ce885f47c5cb11fa7c21f9/src/logging/trace.ts#L265-L305).

## Acceptance criteria

- Reject unsafe trace directories, including symlinks. Create traces with owner-only access where supported and enforce equivalent privacy on other supported platforms.
- Bind writes to the file created for the run and handle directory and file replacement safely. Retain bounded errors and close resources on normal, interrupted, and failed paths.
- Add offline tests for both trace modes that verify regular JSONL output, restrictive permissions where supported, and that redirected or replaced paths leave unrelated files untouched.`}];
store("runtimeIssues",issues);
for(const issue of issues) {
const r = await tools.mcp__codex_apps__github_create_issue({repository_full_name:"petercr/jev-orchestrator",...issue}); text(r);
}
